<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baldwin IV of Jerusalem</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1161–1185</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Leper King</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baldwin IV, known as the Leper King, was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> from 1174. Although he suffered from leprosy from childhood, he led his army in person and defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-montgisard">Battle of Montgisard</a> in 1177. His illness and the factional struggles over the regency and succession weakened the kingdom in the years before its defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hattin">Hattin</a> in 1187.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baldwin-iv-of-jerusalem.jpg" alt="Baldwin IV of Jerusalem" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guillermo de Tiro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Baldwin_IV.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
